  "english": "4. Sunday. Tone 2 [D-Z/d2]. Fifth [Sunday]. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 3 [b3]: \"We glorify You\" (Paravoremk uzkez). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 3 [d3]: \"Foreseeing by the women\" (Pahkanantsn kankhelov).\n5. Monday. Tone 8 [DK/d4]. [Feast of] Eugenios, Macarius, and companions. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 8 [dk/d4]: \"Who the wondrous\" (Vor uzhrashapar).\n6. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AD/a1]. [Feast of] Andrew the General, and his army, etc.\n8. Thursday. Tone 3 [BZ/b1]. [Feast of] Adrian and his wife, etc. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 8 [dk/d4]: \"You the righteous\" (Uzkez artar).\n10. Saturday. Tone 5 [GD/g1]. [Feast of] the Holy Ecumenical Council of Ephesus, the two hundred Patriarchs.\n11. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK/g2]. Sixth [Sunday]. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 8 [dk/d4]: \"Ineffable\" (Anchareli). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk/g2]: \"With the divine tomb\" (Zastvadsayin uzgerezmanavn). Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\n12. Monday. Tone 7 [DD/d1]. Fast of the Holy Mother of God. Father of the Litany of Penitence [Harts-Aghts] Tone 3 [b3]: \"Who art fearsome\" (Vor ahavor).\n18. Sunday. Tone 5 [GD/g1]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The period of non-fasting days [utik] is three weeks. See the First Volume, maintaining the proper order of this place.\nSeptember:\n8. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK/a2]. Fourth [Sunday]. Feast of the Nativity of the Holy Mother of God. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of the Holy Cross.\n9. Monday. Tone 4 [BK/b2]. Fast of the Holy Cross. Father of the Litany of Penitence [Harts-Aghts] Tone 4 [bk/b2]: \"The voice of the children\" (Mankantsn uzdzayn).\n15. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD/a1]. Exaltation of the Holy Cross [Khachverats].\n22. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK/d4]. Second [Sunday]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk/d4]: \"The ranks of angels\" (Hreshtakatsn dask). Barekendan [Eve] of the Cross of Varag.\n23. Monday. Tone 1 [AD/a1]. Fast. [Feast of] Mamas, etc. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 8 [dk/d4]: \"Who art exalted\" (Vor bardzryal).\n25. Wednesday. Tone 4 [BK/b2]. Fast. Father of the Litany of Penitence [Harts-Aghts] Tone 5 [g3]: \"God of our fathers, You...\" (Zhartsn merots astvads uzkez).\n29. Sunday. Tone 7 [DD/d1]. Third [Sunday]. Feast of the Cross of Varag. The period of non-fasting days [utik] is seven weeks. Until the tenth Sunday, see the First Volume, maintaining the proper order of this place.\nOctober:\n6. Sunday. Tone 6 [GK/g2]. Fourth [Sunday]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 6 [gk/g2]: \"Your resurrection\" (Uzko harutiund).\n13. Sunday. Tone 5 [GD/g1]. Fifth [Sunday]. Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 5 [g1]: \"The Oil-bearing women\" (Yughaber), and \"Today is the resurrection\" (Aysor harutiun), and \"With the sign of the cross\" (I khachanish).\nFebruary:\n10. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK/d4]. Great Barekendan [Eve of Great Lent].\n14. Thursday. Tone 4 [BK/b2]. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnundaraj]. See according to the order in the First Volume.\nMarch:\n31. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD/a1]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\nApril:\n7. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK/d4]. New [Sunday]. — Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\nMay:\n9. Thursday. Tone 8 [DK/d4]. Feast of the Ascension of Christ.\n19. Sunday. Tone 2 [AK/a2]. Descent of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Barekendan [Eve] of the Fast of Elijah.\n26. Sunday. Tone 1 [AD/a1]. First Sunday. Beginning of the Sundays of Resurrection. See according to the order in the First Volume.\nJuly:\n7. Sunday. Tone 3 [BZ/b1]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The period of non-fasting days [utik] is five weeks. Until the Friday of the third week, see the First Volume, and on Saturday come here, and celebrate the feasts written below, which are after the eight-day octave of the Nativity.\n27. Saturday. Tone 7 [DD/d1]. [Feast of] the Patriarchs Athanasius and Cyril.\n28. Sunday. Tone 8 [DK/d4]. Fourth [Sunday]. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 4 [bk/b2]: \"Who the heavenly...\" (Vor yerknayin zin). Dismissal Hymn [Hambartsi] Tone 8 [dk/d4]: \"When they came\" (Yorzham yekin), and \"The angel descended\" (Ej hreshtakn).\n29. Monday. Tone 1 [AD/a1]. [Feast of] Cyriacus and Julietta, and Gordius, etc. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 7 [dd/d1]: \"Holy art Thou, Lord of hosts\" (Surb es ter zorutyants).\n30. Tuesday. Tone 2 [AK/a2]. [Feast of] Vahan of Goghtn, and Eugenie the Virgin, etc. Father of the Litany [Harts] Tone 6 [gk/g2]: \"To You, O God\" (Ar kez astvads).\nAugust:\n1. Thursday. Tone 4 [BK/b2]. [Feast of] Tryphon, Parsamas, and Onuphrius the hermits.\n3. Saturday. Tone 6 [GK/g2]. [Feast of] Gregory the Theologian.",
